    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T13:16:35Z",
    "body": "part 1 on issue/743-sim-revolved-tool-body · PR #837 (draft, `Refs`, does not close this issue) · pinned by `crates/app/tests/sim_tool_body.rs` (7 tests: outline equals the laws' band stack, tilted axis, degenerate outline, cache freed on tool/op delete) and the extended ui structural test `the_simulation_draws_the_tool_with_its_holder_cylinder_or_its_body` · merges at the next cut\n\nWhat it does: the simulated tool is one revolved body built from `tool_body::judged` + `tool_body::stack`, the same reads the fixture laws make. A drawn cone is therefore shown as the stepped cylinder the laws judge. Display only, no verdict changed. Not hand-checked on screen.\n\nFound and filed: #835 - the single-cylinder laws (reach, probe) judge the cylinder enclosing a body, wider than the band stack that is drawn.\n\nStill owed here: all of part 2 (STEP body -> editable half-profile stored as DXF with a centreline, direct DXF import, our own DXF read/write with named refusals, the round trip), and the maintainer's hand test of part 1.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
